<%
/* =========================================================================
   ONE PAPER'S SETTINGS — shared by edithomework.ejs, editquiz.ejs and
   editexam.ejs, exactly as _assessment-form.ejs is shared by the three add
   pages. The three edit views were ~400 near-identical lines each and had
   already drifted: only editexam carried start/end time, only editquiz
   carried quizTime, and all three offered a subject select whose values
   ("Secondary" / "Preparatory") match nothing in the database.

   THIS PAGE NO LONGER TOUCHES QUESTIONS, AND THAT IS THE POINT.

   It used to be one form that did both, which made the common job the
   expensive one: an admin who wanted to fix a typo in a quiz's name opened a
   page led by a question builder, scrolled past an empty question block, and
   pressed a save button carrying a question count. Nothing was lost by doing
   that — an empty block is skipped — but the page never said so, and "am I
   about to add a blank question?" is not a question a rename should raise.

   The questions moved to their own page, _manage-questions.ejs, reached from
   the "إدارة الأسئلة" button below and from the list. This form is the
   paper's own fields and a count. Its handler, editPaperPost, does not read a
   question, does not call parseQuestions and has no $push — so renaming a
   paper cannot delete, recreate or re-submit its questions.

   Two consequences worth knowing about:
     · No `enctype`. With the builder gone there is no file input, so the form
       posts as ordinary urlencoded and the route dropped its upload.any().
     · No `.qbuilder`, no `<template data-qtemplate>`, no [data-qadd]. admin.js
       binds the builder by [data-qbuilder] and finds none here, which is the
       correct outcome and not a regression; the hooks all live on the
       questions page now.

   WHICH FIELDS EACH KIND SHOWS
   Quiz and homework: the name, a description, the lesson it is attached to,
   and their one timing field — a duration for a quiz, a due date for a
   homework. The subject and grade selects are gone from BOTH: a paper's
   subject and grade are read off the unit document the chosen lesson lives
   in, so the two can no longer disagree. Setting a paper to biology/3rd while
   its lesson sat under geology/1st used to be one careless save away, and the
   result was a paper that no list would show.

   Exam has no lesson to derive anything from, so it keeps the subject and
   grade selects, plus its start/end window and its per-attempt duration.

   LOCALS
     kind        "homework" | "quiz" | "exam"
     data        the paper
     question    its existing questions (array). Read for `.length` ONLY —
                 the count on the "إدارة الأسئلة" button. Nothing on this page
                 renders a question.
     units       unit documents, for the lesson picker. [] for exam
     currentUnit "docId:rowId" of the row pointing at this paper, or ""
     csrfToken   string
     flashOk / flashBad  strings, may be ""
     formData    a rejected submission to redisplay, or ""

   The question-type locals this file used to need (QTYPES, QTYPE_LABELS and
   the rest of util/questionTypes.viewLocals()) are gone with the builder, and
   editPaperGet deliberately stopped passing them: a local in scope reads as
   "this page deals in question types", which is the invitation that produced
   the combined form in the first place.

   ALL LOCALS ARE READ BEHIND A typeof GUARD. This was the only admin view
   that read `kind`, `data`, `question`, `units`, `currentUnit`, `csrfToken`,
   `flashOk` and `flashBad` bare, and EJS compiles the template body inside
   `with(locals)`: a key the route did not pass is a ReferenceError, not
   undefined. That matters more here than it looks, because a render error is
   thrown from inside res.render's callback — the route's try/catch has already
   returned by then, so Express serves its own 500 and the admin loses the form
   with no message about why. One route that forgets one local takes the whole
   page down; a guard makes it degrade to an empty field instead.
   ====================================================================== */

var KIND = typeof kind !== "undefined" && kind ? String(kind) : "homework";
var paper = typeof data !== "undefined" && data && typeof data === "object" ? data : {};
var unitDocs = typeof units !== "undefined" && Array.isArray(units) ? units : [];
var curUnit = typeof currentUnit !== "undefined" && currentUnit ? String(currentUnit) : "";
var tok = typeof csrfToken !== "undefined" && csrfToken ? csrfToken : "";
var ok = typeof flashOk !== "undefined" && flashOk ? String(flashOk) : "";
var bad = typeof flashBad !== "undefined" && flashBad ? String(flashBad) : "";

var LABEL = { homework: "الواجب", quiz: "الكويز", exam: "الامتحان" }[KIND] || "الواجب";
var PLURAL = { homework: "الواجبات", quiz: "الكويزات", exam: "الامتحانات" }[KIND] || "الواجبات";
var LIST_HREF = "/admin/" + KIND;
var EDIT_HREF = { homework: "/editHomework", quiz: "/editQuiz", exam: "/editExam" }[KIND] || "/editHomework";

/* The other half of the split. One href, used by the header button and by the
   empty state, so there is one route name to keep in step with the routers. */
var QUESTIONS_HREF = {
  homework: "/questionsOfHomework",
  quiz: "/questionsOfQuiz",
  exam: "/questionsOfExam"
}[KIND] || "/questionsOfHomework";

var isExam = KIND === "exam";
var isHomework = KIND === "homework";

/* A rejected submission comes back through flash. Every failure path
   redirects — correct, so a refresh cannot resubmit — but a redirect renders a
   blank form, and blanking a description because the name was left empty is
   not a usable way to work. Falls back to the stored paper when there is
   nothing to restore. */
var prior = typeof formData !== "undefined" && formData && typeof formData === "object" ? formData : null;

function was(key, fallback) {
  if (prior && prior[key] !== undefined && prior[key] !== null && prior[key] !== "") {
    return String(prior[key]);
  }
  return fallback === undefined || fallback === null ? "" : String(fallback);
}

/* The count, and nothing more. `question` is the array of stored questions and
   this page reads exactly one thing from it. */
var existing = typeof question !== "undefined" && Array.isArray(question) ? question : [];

/* Only exam reads these. Quiz and homework take their subject and grade from
   the unit document the chosen lesson lives in — see editPaperPost. */
var curSubject = was("educetionlevel", paper.educetionlevel);
var curGrade = was("grade", paper.grade);

/* ------------------------------------------- the lesson placement picker ---
   Unit rows grouped by subject / grade / month so a long list is navigable.
   Rows already pointing at a DIFFERENT paper are disabled: editPaperPost
   refuses them, and offering them anyway is how a save appeared to work and
   changed nothing.

   Built up here, in the shape _field.ejs consumes, rather than in the template
   body where it used to sit. The add form builds the same list the same way,
   and the two were the pair that drifted the furthest — this one had lost
   `input--ltr`, `dir="ltr"` and `required` on the time fields and carried the
   short grade labels the rest of the dashboard had already dropped.

   The "(مشغول)" note is folded into the label because an <option> holds text,
   not markup — a suffix is part of the label however it is written in source. */
var PLACE_SUBJECTS = { biology: "الأحياء", geology: "الجيولوجيا" };
var PLACE_GRADES = { "1st": "الصف الأول", "2nd": "الصف الثاني", "3rd": "الصف الثالث" };

var placeGroups = [];
var placeSeen = {};
var linkField = KIND === "quiz" ? "quizId" : "homeId";

for (var d = 0; d < unitDocs.length; d++) {
  var doc = unitDocs[d] || {};
  var docRows = Array.isArray(doc.units) ? doc.units : [];
  for (var u = 0; u < docRows.length; u++) {
    var row = docRows[u] || {};
    var rowValue = String(doc._id) + ":" + String(row._id);
    var occupied = !!(row[linkField] && String(row[linkField]) !== String(paper._id));

    var head =
      (PLACE_SUBJECTS[doc.educetionlevel] || doc.educetionlevel || "—") +
      " · " +
      (PLACE_GRADES[doc.grade] || doc.grade || "—") +
      " · " +
      (row.month || "بدون شهر");

    if (!placeSeen[head]) {
      placeSeen[head] = { label: head, items: [] };
      placeGroups.push(placeSeen[head]);
    }
    placeSeen[head].items.push({
      value: rowValue,
      label: (row.unit || "بدون اسم") + (occupied ? " (مشغول)" : ""),
      disabled: occupied
    });
  }
}

/* currentUnit is the row this paper is already attached to; a rejected
   submission's choice wins over it. */
var priorUnit = prior ? was("unitPlacement", curUnit) : curUnit;

/* Both paths are the ones _manage-questions.ejs uses for the same two tabs.
   They have to match: the bar renders on both halves, so an icon that differs
   between them makes the two tabs look like four. */
var ICON = {
  info: "M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8l-6-6Zm2 16H8v-2h8v2Zm0-4H8v-2h8v2Zm-3-5V3.5L18.5 9H13Z",
  list: "M4 6h2v2H4V6Zm4 0h12v2H8V6ZM4 11h2v2H4v-2Zm4 0h12v2H8v-2ZM4 16h2v2H4v-2Zm4 0h12v2H8v-2Z"
};
%>

<%
/* Class names are the ones _assessment-form.ejs already uses, because
   admin.css already styles those. This partial originally invented a
   parallel set — .notice, .card, .card__title, .empty, .btn--primary — none
   of which exist in the stylesheet, so the whole page rendered as unstyled
   flow content: full-bleed text, no card, no spacing, no responsive grid.
   .crumbs and .split-nav below are the only genuinely new components. */
%>
<% if (ok) { %>
<p class="flash flash--ok" role="status"><%= ok %></p>
<% } %>
<% if (bad) { %>
<p class="flash flash--bad" role="alert"><%= bad %></p>
<% } %>

<%
/* The crumbs are the same shape as every other detail page — link, separator,
   the thing you are looking at. They used to be a single link prefixed with
   `&#8592;` (←), which points the wrong way on an RTL page: "back" runs
   rightwards here, so the arrow sent the eye away from the link it belonged to.
   Dropping it rather than mirroring it is the better fix — the trail already
   says where you are, and an arrow that has to be reasoned about is one job too
   many for a separator. */
%>
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="مسار التنقل">
  <a href="<%= LIST_HREF %>">كل <%= PLURAL %></a>
  <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
  <span><%= paper.nameQuiz || LABEL %></span>
</nav>

<%
/* THE SPLIT, STATED ON THE PAGE. Two jobs, and the admin is on one of them.

   This bar is deliberately above the form rather than tucked into the actions
   row at the bottom: someone who came here to work on the questions needs to
   find that out before filling anything in, not after saving. The current page
   is marked with aria-current and is not a link — a link to where you already
   are is a dead end that reads as a choice.

   The count is the whole reason the `question` local is still passed. It is
   orientation, not content: "this paper has 12 questions" tells the admin
   whether the other page is worth opening. */
%>
<nav class="split-nav" aria-label="تعديل <%= LABEL %>">
  <span class="split-nav__item is-current" aria-current="page">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="<%= ICON.info %>" />
    </svg>
    بيانات <%= LABEL %>
  </span>
  <a class="split-nav__item" href="<%= QUESTIONS_HREF %>/<%= paper._id %>">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="<%= ICON.list %>" />
    </svg>
    إدارة الأسئلة
    <span class="split-nav__count num" dir="ltr"><%= existing.length %></span>
  </a>
</nav>

<section class="form-card">
  <h2 class="form-card__title">بيانات <%= LABEL %></h2>
  <p class="form-card__lede">
    عدّل بيانات <%= LABEL %> وإعداداته. الأسئلة تُدار من صفحة «إدارة الأسئلة»
    ولا يتأثر أي سؤال بالحفظ هنا.
  </p>

  <%
  /* No enctype. There is no file input on this form any more, so it posts as
     ordinary urlencoded — which is also why the route dropped upload.any() and
     csrfProtect went back to running first. */
  %>
  <form method="post" action="<%= EDIT_HREF %>/<%= paper._id %>">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= tok %>" />

    <%
    /* The same includes the add form uses, in the same order, which is the
       point of the exercise: this page and _assessment-form.ejs are two states
       of one form and every difference between them below is now deliberate
       and visible in one screen of code, instead of spread over 150 lines of
       markup that had to be compared by eye. */
    %>
    <div class="form-grid">
      <%- include("_field", { fld: {
        type: "text", name: "nameQuiz", id: "nameQuiz",
        label: "اسم " + LABEL, value: was("nameQuiz", paper.nameQuiz),
        required: true, full: true, maxlength: 120, autocomplete: "off"
      } }) %>

      <%
      /* PAPER-level free text: what it covers, how to approach it, what to
         revise first. Optional, and empty on every paper created before the
         field existed — which is why the controller writes it only when it is
         posted, and never invents one.

         maxlength matches MAX_DESCRIPTION in the controller, so the browser
         stops at the same number the server rejects at. The server rejects
         rather than truncating: a form-driven save can never reach the limit,
         so anything that does is a hand-built POST, and silently rewriting one
         into something the admin never typed is the worse failure. */
      %>
      <%- include("_field", { fld: {
        type: "textarea", name: "description", id: "description",
        label: "وصف " + LABEL, value: was("description", paper.description),
        full: true, tall: true, rows: 4, maxlength: 500,
        hint: "اختياري — نبذة قصيرة عمّا يغطيه " + LABEL + " تظهر للمدرّس في لوحة التحكم."
      } }) %>

      <% if (isExam) { %>
      <%
      /* Exam only. An exam belongs to no lesson, so there is nothing to derive
         its subject and grade from and they have to be picked here.

         The values are biology / geology, from _field.ejs's presets. The old
         select offered "Secondary" and "Preparatory" — which are grade stages,
         not subjects, and match no paper, no student and no query. Saving the
         form without touching this field rewrote the paper's subject to a value
         nothing looks for, and it vanished from the student lists.

         Both selects now carry the neutral option they lacked. Without one, a
         paper whose stored value is not in the list rendered with the FIRST
         option selected and no indication of it, and the next save wrote that
         over the real value; _field.ejs surfaces the stray value instead, and
         `required` stops the form until a real one is chosen. */
      %>
      <%- include("_field", { fld: {
        type: "select", name: "educetionlevel", id: "educetionlevel",
        label: "المادة", list: "levels", value: curSubject, required: true
      } }) %>

      <%- include("_field", { fld: {
        type: "select", name: "grade", id: "grade", label: "الصف",
        list: "grades", value: curGrade, required: true
      } }) %>
      <% } %>

      <% if (!isExam) { %>
      <%
      /* `neutral` is spelled out here instead of taking the default
         "اختر الدرس المرتبط…", because on this one select the empty option is
         not "you have not chosen yet" — it is a real choice that detaches the
         paper from its lesson. It needs to say so. (The wording it replaces,
         "— بدون —", was one of five different spellings of the empty option
         across the dashboard, and the only one that meant something.)

         `unknown: false`: the value is an opaque docId:rowId pair, so echoing
         back a stale one would show the admin two dozen hex characters and a
         label telling them it is unrecognised. "Not attached" is the honest
         reading of a placement that no longer exists. */
      %>
      <%- include("_field", { fld: {
        type: "select", name: "unitPlacement", id: "unitPlacement",
        label: "الدرس المرتبط", list: placeGroups, value: priorUnit,
        full: true, unknown: false, neutral: "بدون درس مرتبط",
        hint: "اختر درسًا لربط " + LABEL + " به. الدروس المشغولة بـ" + (KIND === "quiz" ? "كويز" : "واجب") + " آخر معطّلة."
      } }) %>
      <% } %>

      <% if (isExam) { %>
      <%
      /* `required`, matching the add form. An exam is defined by when it opens
         and closes — that is the whole difference between an exam and a
         homework here — and the add form has always demanded both. This page
         did not, so an exam could be saved with an empty window from the edit
         side only, and an exam with no window is one no student can be shown at
         the right time. A legacy exam missing a window now has to be given one
         before other edits can be saved, which is the intended consequence:
         the form asks for the thing that was always required and never
         enforced. */
      %>
      <%- include("_field", { fld: {
        type: "datetime-local", name: "startTime", id: "startTime",
        label: "يفتح في", value: was("startTime", paper.startTime),
        required: true, width: "md"
      } }) %>

      <%- include("_field", { fld: {
        type: "datetime-local", name: "endTime", id: "endTime",
        label: "يغلق في", value: was("endTime", paper.endTime),
        required: true, width: "md"
      } }) %>
      <% } %>

      <% if (isHomework) { %>
      <%
      /* Homework only, and INFORMATIONAL. It is recorded and displayed; it does
         not lock anything. routes/homework.router.js deliberately reports every
         homework as state "untimed" with opensAt/closesAt null, and a due date
         that silently started closing homework would change what students can
         open — a bigger decision than "add a field to the edit form", and one
         that would have been made by accident if this had been stored in
         `endTime` instead. It has its own field for exactly that reason: see
         the comment on dueDate in models/quiz.js.

         Not required: a homework without a due date is the normal case and was
         the only case until this field existed. */
      %>
      <%- include("_field", { fld: {
        type: "datetime-local", name: "dueDate", id: "dueDate",
        label: "موعد التسليم", value: was("dueDate", paper.dueDate),
        width: "md",
        hint: "اختياري. للعلم فقط — لا يُغلق " + LABEL + " تلقائيًا في هذا الموعد."
      } }) %>
      <% } %>

      <% if (!isHomework) { %>
      <%
      /* Duration — a quiz's time limit, an exam's per-attempt allowance. The
         same field on the document (quizTime) and the same control on both
         forms, which is why this branch is "not homework" rather than two
         copies; homework has no duration at all.

         THIS FIELD WAS MISSING FROM THE QUIZ EDIT FORM, and the reason is worth
         keeping: cleanQuizTime(undefined) returns "", so writing the duration
         unconditionally untimed every quiz that was saved from a form not
         carrying the field. The fix at the time was to stop writing it, which
         made it uneditable — settable when a quiz was created and never again.
         editPaperPost now guards on `typeof req.body.quizTime === "string"`, so
         posted-and-empty clears it and absent leaves it alone, and the field can
         come back.

         NOT required, deliberately: the add form leaves it optional and says so
         in its hint. Requiring it here would invent a new add/edit difference
         while closing an old one.

         placeholder, not value. The old field shipped value="hh:mm" as its
         DEFAULT, so an untouched form stored the literal string "hh:mm", the
         duration parsed as NaN and the paper was silently untimed. */
      %>
      <%- include("_field", { fld: {
        type: "text", name: "quizTime", id: "quizTime", label: "مدة " + LABEL,
        value: was("quizTime", paper.quizTime), width: "sm", ltr: true,
        inputmode: "numeric", pattern: "[0-9]{1,2}:[0-9]{2}",
        placeholder: "00:30", autocomplete: "off",
        hintHtml: 'بصيغة ساعات:دقائق، مثل <span class="num" dir="ltr">00:30</span>. اتركه فارغًا لجعله بلا وقت.'
      } }) %>
      <% } %>
    </div>

    <%
    /* "حفظ" here, "حفظ" on addStudent and "حفظ التعديلات" on editStudent were
       one action under three names. The shared default, "حفظ التغييرات", is
       what every save on the dashboard says now; the add pages pass their own
       "إضافة …" because creating a thing genuinely is a different action.

       NO `badge`. The badge is the question builder's [data-qcount] pill, and
       there is no builder on this page — a count on this save button would be
       claiming that pressing it does something to the questions, which is the
       exact confusion the split removes. The note says the opposite out loud.

       The cancel link was "رجوع" pointing at the list. It is "إلغاء" now, the
       same word as everywhere else, and the crumbs above are what "back" means
       on this page. */
    %>
    <%- include("_form-actions", { act: {
      cancel: LIST_HREF,
      note: "يحفظ بيانات " + LABEL + " فقط — الأسئلة لا تتغيّر."
    } }) %>
  </form>
</section>
